summary: Working on metafolder itself — building it, testing it, the static checks, measuring performance, and the rules a change must follow.

metafolder is a Cargo workspace of seven crates plus a Svelte frontend and this
wiki ([[Architecture]]). Everything needed to work on it is a script under
`scripts/` or a plain `cargo` command.

A change goes through the same steps whatever it touches:

# ''The test first.'' Write it, see it fail, then write the code ([[Testing conventions]]).
# ''Build'' — `cargo build` for one crate's work, `scripts/complete-build.sh` when the frontend, the documentation or the installed configuration are involved ([[Building]]).
# ''Check'' — `scripts/check.sh` runs the formatter, the lints, every test suite and the project's own invariants in one pass ([[Static checks]]).
# ''Measure'', when the change could cost something — `scripts/bench.sh` compares against what this machine measured before ([[Performance testing]]).
# ''Say it'' — the note that describes the behaviour changes with the code ([[Writing documentation]]), the wire version moves if an older client would misbehave ([[The wire protocol version]]), and data already on disk is converted, never broken ([[Persisted format changes]]).
# ''Commit'' — one feature, one commit, once it is built, green and formatted (`cargo fmt --all`).

What must stay true across all of it is listed in [[Key invariants]].

